<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <RootNamespace>MUI.Web.Tests</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>MUI.Web.Tests</AssemblyName>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <IsTestProject>true</IsTestProject>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="TUnit" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    So a test can render a component to HTML with the framework's own HtmlRenderer and assert on
    what came out. Claims about markup — that the heatmap is a real table with headers, that a
    hatched hour is a different element from an empty one — are only worth anything when they are
    read off a rendered frame rather than off the source. No package: this is in the shared
    framework the web project already targets.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <FrameworkReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.App" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\MUI.Web\MUI.Web.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    The English bundle as a translator edits it, copied beside the test binary.

    A test here compares Messages.resx against the compiled-in source dictionary, and it has to read
    the *file* to do it: going through the resource manager would read whatever the build embedded,
    which is the thing under test. It used to find the file by counting five ".." segments up from
    AppContext.BaseDirectory, which is only the repository root when the output sits at exactly
    bin/<config>/<tfm> — so a redirected output path, an artifacts layout, a second target framework
    or a different configuration nesting each turned a message-content test into a
    FileNotFoundException naming a path nobody recognised.

    MSBuild resolves this relative to the project file, which is a fixed relationship rather than a
    guess about where the output landed, and the copy is the same bytes. Searching upward for the
    repository root would have worked too and still assumes the output is inside the repository.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\..\src\MUI.Web\Resources\Messages.resx"
          Link="Messages.resx"
          CopyToOutputDirectory="PreserveNewest" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
